            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Benjamin J. Butler, petitioner argues that the Minnesota Supreme Court incorrectly held that this Court prevented it from deciding which state prisoners may bring federal constitutional challenges in Minnesota courts."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Benjamin J. Butler",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c76faf93c4d835c3eb143a6106bc3d71187abf7ef04eaff61d79bd200fb077b8",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c76faf93c4d8-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Benjamin J. Butler, petitioner also contends that the Teague Court imposed procedural and prudential limits on a defense available to the State in habeas corpus."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Benjamin J. Butler",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c76faf93c4d835c3eb143a6106bc3d71187abf7ef04eaff61d79bd200fb077b8",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c76faf93c4d8-0000-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 13,
              "start": 13
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Benjamin J. Butler, petitioner references the Hudson case concerning Fourth Amendment no\u2011knock violations."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c76faf93c4d835c3eb143a6106bc3d71187abf7ef04eaff61d79bd200fb077b8",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c76faf93c4d8-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 33,
              "start": 33
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Souter, justice Souter inquired about the finality point and its effect on uniform application of a rule across states."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c76faf93c4d835c3eb143a6106bc3d71187abf7ef04eaff61d79bd200fb077b8",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c76faf93c4d8-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kennedy, justice Kennedy expressed serious problems with the petitioner's position."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c76faf93c4d835c3eb143a6106bc3d71187abf7ef04eaff61d79bd200fb077b8",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c76faf93c4d8-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Breyer asked whether the issue is a matter of federal law."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c76faf93c4d835c3eb143a6106bc3d71187abf7ef04eaff61d79bd200fb077b8",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c76faf93c4d8-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 48,
              "start": 47
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Stevens asked whether the Teague rule originates from the Court's power to create federal common law or from a constitutional mandate."
      }
    ],
